Room: Room's content-blocking agent joins every renderer frame.

Room blocks ads and trackers itself (B-30; research/notes/adblock-approach.md,
option c, the user's decision 2026-10-17). Hiding elements, scriptlets and
cookie-banner handling have to happen inside each document before its own
scripts run, which takes a content::RenderFrameObserver per frame: the
browser pushes each document's resources over the frame's associated
interfaces at ReadyToCommitNavigation (subresource_filter's push model) and
the agent applies them at DidCreateDocumentElement.

No existing hook: RenderFrameObservers are created only by the
ContentRendererClient (ChromeContentRendererClient::RenderFrameCreated);
subclassing it would replace Chrome's for one call. //room sets the hook
from a static initializer when the framework loads in a renderer, as it
does for patch 0007's media hook.

2026-10-17. //room: room/core/content_blocking/cosmetic_filter_agent.cc.
diff --git a/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc b/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
index d460c0fb699d6..a9d38544c7f2e 100644
--- a/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc
@@ -649,8 +649,18 @@ void ChromeContentRendererClient::ExposeInterfacesToBrowser(
   ExposeChromeRendererInterfacesToBrowser(this, binders);
 }
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core when the framework loads in a renderer. Gives
+// each frame Room's content-blocking agent (cosmetic filters, scriptlets,
+// cookie banners; B-30).
+void (*g_render_frame_created_hook)(content::RenderFrame*) = nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 void ChromeContentRendererClient::RenderFrameCreated(
     content::RenderFrame* render_frame) {
+  if (room::g_render_frame_created_hook) {
+    room::g_render_frame_created_hook(render_frame);
+  }
   ChromeRenderFrameObserver* render_frame_observer =
       new ChromeRenderFrameObserver(render_frame, web_cache_impl_.get());
   service_manager::BinderRegistry* registry = render_frame_observer->registry();
